                        "entry_id": "c90d55e3-cf58-30b8-8c81-fdbf036c1eb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Finger-like."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a43155cd-da00-472d-8bb3-ca45955af6e4",
                                "sense_id": "1ea2a1a6-af8a-3deb-9d3a-484899fdf2d5",
                                "text": "Distinguished by its elongated dactylose form, and by the bold longitudinally striped pattern of the epidermis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5fefa47-ef05-4a17-843c-bdecdf2efab9",
                                "sense_id": "1ea2a1a6-af8a-3deb-9d3a-484899fdf2d5",
                                "text": "It consists of a little calcareous cylindrical column, about one tenth of an inch in height, attached by a dactylose base, and surmounted by an expansion in the form of a reversed cone, the margin of whose wide end is extended into several radiating arms, which, like the rest of the fossil, are entirely calcareous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e545fd8-44ca-4c5c-a5d8-bc95311fca39",
                                "sense_id": "1ea2a1a6-af8a-3deb-9d3a-484899fdf2d5",
                                "text": "In front of them on the ventral surface is a pair of short dactylose processes, bluntly rounded at their tips; the abdomen is lacking."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
